WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.416 --> 00:00:02.256
Good morning!

2
00:00:02.436 --> 00:00:03.817
[s@Good morning!

3
00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:04.697
Who are you?

4
00:00:04.717 --> 00:00:06.297
I'm a groundhog.

5
00:00:06.557 --> 00:00:09.718
Groundhogs are big rodents.

6
00:00:09.758 --> 00:00:11.919
We're also called woodchucks.

7
00:00:33.248 --> 00:00:34.269
Where do you live?

8
00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:37.772
We live near fields and meadows.

9
00:00:39.473 --> 00:00:41.955
We usually stay close to forests.

10
00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:45.418
What do you eat?

11
00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:49.662
We like grasses, plants, and fruit.

12
00:00:51.143 --> 00:00:54.686
Sometimes we eat tree bark or bugs too.

13
00:00:57.068 --> 00:00:58.469
You eat a lot!

14
00:00:58.489 --> 00:01:02.172
We eat a lot in summer and fall.

15
00:01:03.704 --> 00:01:06.086
But we don't eat during winter.

16
00:01:08.248 --> 00:01:11.131
Groundhogs hibernate all winter long.

17
00:01:13.913 --> 00:01:15.614
Do you ever climb trees?

18
00:01:17.416 --> 00:01:20.358
Yes. We climb trees and bushes.

19
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.701
We can swim too.

20
00:01:25.903 --> 00:01:27.284
Who are your enemies?

21
00:01:28.926 --> 00:01:30.887
Bears and foxes hunt us.

22
00:01:32.764 --> 00:01:34.805
So do wolves and birds.

23
00:01:36.425 --> 00:01:38.886
We hide from enemies underground.

24
00:01:40.726 --> 00:01:41.967
Do you dig holes?

25
00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:46.448
Yes! Groundhogs are good diggers.

26
00:01:48.428 --> 00:01:51.349
We use our claws to dig deep holes.

27
00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:55.450
Our holes have rooms and tunnels.

28
00:01:59.512 --> 00:02:00.552
Here comes a fox.

29
00:02:02.496 --> 00:02:03.439
Time to hide!

30
00:02:05.644 --> 00:02:06.846
Good-bye, Groundhog!
